0: {'E': 7.6, 'P': 3.5, 'L': 8.4, 'E_Expl': 'Jim Lehrer establishes his credibility as the moderator by mentioning his position and the sponsoring organization.', 'P_Expl': "The audience's applause creates an emotional response to welcome the candidates.", 'L_Expl': 'Lehrer provides a logical introduction by outlining the debate format, topics, and rules.', 'E_Clauses': {'1': 'I’m Jim Lehrer of the NewsHour on PBS', '2': 'the Commission on Presidential Debates is the sponsor of this event'}, 'P_Clauses': {'1': '(APPLAUSE) Let me begin with something General Eisenhower said in his 1952 presidential campaign.'}, 'L_Clauses': {'1': 'Tonight’s will primarily be about foreign policy and national security, which, by definition, includes the global financial crisis.', '2': 'It will be divided roughly into nine-minute segments.', '3': 'Direct exchanges between the candidates and moderator follow-ups are permitted after each candidate has two minutes to answer the lead question in an order determined by a coin toss.', '4': 'The specific subjects and questions were chosen by me. They have not been shared or cleared with anyone.'}}
5: {'E': 7.5, 'P': 6.2, 'L': 8.2, 'E_Expl': 'The speaker establishes credibility by sharing past actions addressing the problem.', 'P_Expl': "An appeal to the audience's hope for solving the problem is made by expressing optimism.", 'L_Expl': 'The speaker uses logical analysis to explain the reasons behind the current situation and proposes a new regulatory framework.', 'E_Clauses': {'1': 'Two years ago, I warned that...', '2': 'Last year, I wrote to the secretary of the Treasury...'}, 'P_Clauses': {'1': 'I am optimistic about the capacity of us to come together with a plan.'}, 'L_Clauses': {'1': 'How did we get into this situation in the first place?', '2': 'But we’re also going to have to look at, how is it that we shredded so many regulations?', '3': 'We did not set up a 21st-century regulatory framework to deal with these problems.'}}
1: {'E': 7.4, 'P': 8.4, 'L': 8.0, 'E_Expl': 'The speaker establishes credibility by thanking the host and acknowledging the importance of the debate.', 'P_Expl': 'The speaker evokes emotion by addressing the financial struggles and concerns of the audience.', 'L_Expl': 'The speaker presents logical arguments and specific proposals for addressing the financial crisis.', 'E_Clauses': {'1': 'Well, thank you very much, Jim, and thanks to the commission and the University of Mississippi,', '2': 'Ole Miss, for hosting us tonight.'}, 'P_Clauses': {'1': 'And although we’ve heard a lot about Wall Street, those of you on Main Street I think have been struggling for a while, and you recognize that this could have an impact on all sectors of the economy.', '2': 'And you’re wondering, how’s it going to affect me?'}, 'L_Clauses': {'1': 'So we have to move swiftly, and we have to move wisely.', '2': 'And I’ve put forward a series of proposals that make sure that we protect taxpayers as we engage in this important rescue effort.', '3': 'Number one, we’ve got to make sure that we’ve got oversight over this whole process;', '4': '$700 billion, potentially, is a lot of money. Number two, we’ve got to make sure that taxpayers, when they are putting their money at risk, have the possibility of getting that money back and gains, if the market — and when the market returns.', '5': 'Number three, we’ve got to make sure that none of that money is going to pad CEO bank accounts or to promote golden parachutes.', '6': 'And, number four, we’ve got to make sure that we’re helping homeowners, because the root problem here has to do with the foreclosures that are taking place all across the country.'}}
3: {'E': 6.4, 'P': 7.2, 'L': 7.8, 'E_Expl': 'The speaker references their personal experiences and expresses empathy.', 'P_Expl': 'The speaker evokes emotions through discussing the struggles of everyday Americans.', 'L_Expl': 'The speaker provides logical arguments for the proposed package and its benefits.', 'E_Clauses': {'1': 'Senator Kennedy is in the hospital. He’s a dear and beloved friend to all of us.', '2': 'I’ve been around a little while.'}, 'P_Clauses': {'1': 'We’re not talking about failure of institutions on Wall Street. We’re talking about failures on Main Street, and people who will lose their jobs, and their credits, and their homes, if we don’t fix the greatest fiscal crisis.', '2': 'This isn’t the beginning of the end of this crisis. This is the end of the beginning, if we come out with a package that will keep these institutions stable.'}, 'L_Clauses': {'1': 'Because as we’re here tonight in this debate, we are seeing, for the first time in a long time, Republicans and Democrats together, sitting down, trying to work out a solution to this fiscal crisis that we’re in.', '2': 'This package has transparency in it. It has to have accountability and oversight. It has to have options for loans to failing businesses, rather than the government taking over those loans.', '3': 'if we come out with a package that will keep these institutions stable. And we’ve got a lot of work to do. And we’ve got to create jobs. And one of the areas, of course, is to eliminate our dependence on foreign oil.'}}
